  "checked": "2026 WC semi, 15 July, Atlanta: Gordon put England 1-0 up (55'), Enzo Fernández curled in Messi's pass (85'), Lautaro Martínez headed in Messi's cross in stoppage time; 1-2 (Sports Mole, Outlook India, Quotidiano). Messi born 24 June 1987, so 39. Debut 17 Aug 2005 v Hungary, sent off about a minute after coming on (CBS, beIN). Lost the 2014 WC, 2015 and 2016 Copa finals, quit Argentina after the 2016 final, then came back (Dawn, The National). Titles: Copa 2021, Finalissima 2022, WC 2022, Copa 2024 (beIN, Copa America, UEFA). England: Euro 2020 final lost on pens to Italy, Euro 2024 final lost 2-1 to Spain, no senior trophy since 1966 (Sporting Life, Al Jazeera, 11v11). The England-Messi scenes are clearly imagined. Kits in the game footage are plain: the game's figures can't draw Argentina's stripes.",
